  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support access of vulnerable groups</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Implement integration activities to close gaps in community outreach and strengthen the capacity of provincial health workers;
&#x2022; Quickly implementation with a team of Oxfam and government partners who have a deep understanding of the local context, with a team in the project target areas, and highly skilled technical staff.
&#x2022; Strengthen local organizations through partnerships with local leaders and partners to the application of locally relevant approaches.
&#x2022; Implement the activities according to the plan stated in theMOU, under the supervision of Department of Hygiene and Health Promotion, and Provincial Health Department of respective target provinces.
&#x2022; Association for Rural Mobilization and Improvement (ARMI) is responsible for project implementation and coordination with local authorities in districts of Savannakhet province.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association for Rural Mobilisation and Improvement (ARMI) is a Nationwide Membership Lao Civil Society Organization that was established in 2006 under the Lao Union of Science and Engineering Associations (LUSEA) and re-registered under the Ministryof Home Affairs (MoHA) license No. 511/MoHA on August 12, 2012.
In May 2005, at the Lao member organization (LMO) meeting, it was discussed and agreed that &quot;the CIDSE-Laos office needs to close by the end of 2008&quot;. Following that agreement, CIDSE-Laos&#x2019; staff has held many follow-up discussions. On April 3-4, the last workshop was held in the CIDSE Laos office. Fifteen CIDSE staff decided to set up a membership association registered under the Lao Union of Science and Engineering Associations (LUSEA) on October 10, 2006.

ARMI was re-registered on August 9, 2012, under the Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA) and changed its name to &quot;Association for Rural Mobilization andImprovement (ARMI)&quot; in order to fit the decree No. 115/PM on the establishment of the association in Laos, which was approved on April 29, 2009.

Vision:
ARMI aims to contribute to the well-being of all-ethnic groups based on mutual respect, equal opportunities, care for the environment, and the sustainable use of resources.

Mission:
To build capacities amongst target groups to improve theirquality of life for their well-being in green and sustainable ways.

Target group:
Rural communities and the poor and disadvantaged, especially children, youth, women, and people with disabilities (PWDs).

Values: Solidarity, Participation, Transparency, Effectiveness, and Opportunities for All

5 Years of Strategic Goals (2021-2025):
1. To reduce poverty by improving food security
2. To promote nutrition and sanitation for good health for all in communities
3. To protect the environment and natural resources in green andsustainable ways
4. To promote community participation for the quality of education
5. To promote community development with the participation of PWDs</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association for Rural Mobilisation</narrative>
